    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="10.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IIAs">II As</ref> 10.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="156" ed="#liebermann"/>Be wore<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.6"/> gewitnesse. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.1"/> þonne afinde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="**" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.star2"/><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.7"/>, þæt heora<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.8"/> ænig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.9"/> on wore<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.6"/> gewitnesse wære, þæt næfre his gewitnes eft noht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.1"/> ne forstonde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.10"/>; ⁊ eac gesylle<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.4"/> XXX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-ld"><pb n="156" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif mon ðonne onfinde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> heora ænig on fore<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.2"/> gewitnysse sy, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> his gewitnysse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.2"/> næfre eft nawht ne forstande; ⁊ gesylle eac XXX scill. to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-ot"><pb n="156" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif man<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3a" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.3a"/> þon<hi rend="italic">ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.1-2"/></hi> onfinde, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> heora ænig on wore [gewitnesse sie], þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> his gewitnes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.4-2"/> næfre eft nauht ne forst[ande]; ⁊<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.5"/> geselle eac XXX scill' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="157" ed="#liebermann"/>Si autem pernoscatur, quod eorum aliquis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.8-2"/> in falso testimonio sit, eius testimonium deinceps<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.9-2"/> numquam prestet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.10-2"/> aliquid; et etiam emendet XXX sol. (et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.11"/> habeat dominus illam cambitionem).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" n="10.1" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="132" ed="#attenborough"/>Be wore<ptr type="editorNote" n="21" target="#IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.21"/> gewitnesse. Gif mon þonne afinde<ptr type="editorNote" n="22" target="#IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.22"/>, þæt heora ænig on wore<ptr type="editorNote" n="23" target="#IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.23"/> gewitnesse wære<ptr type="editorNote" n="24" target="#IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.24"/>, þæt næfre his gewitnes eft noht<ptr type="editorNote" n="25" target="#IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.25"/> ne forstonde; ⁊ eac gesylle XXX scll' to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="157" ed="#liebermann"/>(Über falsches Zeugniss. <hi rend="italic">H</hi>) Wenn man aber herausfindet, dass einer von jenen in falschem Zeugniss<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.de.1"/> gewesen ist: dass niemals<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.de.2"/> wieder sein Zeugniss etwas gelte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#IIAs_10-1.lnote.de.3"/>; und er zahle auch [dem König] 30 Schill. zur Strafe.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(On false witness. H) But if it is found out that any of them has been in false witness: that his witness shall never again count for anything; and let him also pay [the king] 30 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="133" ed="#attenborough"/>But if it is found that any one of them has borne false witness, never again shall his witness be valid; and moreover he shall pay a fine of 30 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="420" ed="#whitelock"/>Concerning false witness. If it is then discovered that any of them gave false witness, his witness is never again to be valid; and also he is to pay 30 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_37">II Cn 37</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">Ld's ‘on fore’ for ‘on wore’ (false); Liebermann thinks Ot and Ld's ‘onfinde’ more original than H's ‘afinde’.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sic</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> wohre</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to wohre</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.star2" n="**" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">originaler</hi> onfinde <hi rend="italic">laut Ot Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">onfinde more original, according to Ot Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">a <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">a on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eo <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eo on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æ <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æ on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd.</hi> -stande</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered to -stande</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">157</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-uid <hi rend="italic">MHk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-uid MHk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.9-2" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">157</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">n. d. <hi rend="italic">MHkBr</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">n. d. MHkBr</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.10-2" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">157</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">prestetur alicui <hi rend="italic">Br</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">prestetur alicui Br</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">157</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">et — camb. <hi rend="italic">in OrRTMHkBr, fehlt K</hi> [<hi rend="italic">besser: ursprüngliche Übersetzung zum Ende vorigen Satzes, hierher verschoben</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">et — camb. in OrRTMHkBr, lacking in K [better: originally the translation of the end of the preceding sentence, moved here]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.3a" n="3a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">mon <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">mon So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.1-2" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ausgeschrieben So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">written out in full So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.4-2" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-nesse <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-nesse So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.oe.5" n="5" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">156</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl ebd.;</hi> Zeugen 5 a. c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl ibid.;</hi> Zeugen 5 a. c</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl ebd.;</hi> Zeugen 5 a. c</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl ibid.;</hi> Zeugen 5 a. c</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">104</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Q übs. silbenhaft <hi rend="italic">for-stande: præ-stet.</hi> — Für falsches Zeugnis wie für falsche Klage (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7-e) trifft den Verleumder die Strafe, die bei Richtigkeit Verklagten getroffen hätte</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q translates syllable by syllable <hi rend="italic">for-stande: præ-stet.</hi> — For false witness, as for false accusation (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7-e), the slanderer incurs the penalty that would have befallen the accused had the charge been true</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.21" n="21" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><label>wore</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">Altered to <hi rend="italic">wohre</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.22" n="22" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><label>afinde</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">onfinde</hi>. Ld, Ot.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.23" n="23" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><label>wore</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">fore</hi>. Ld.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.24" n="24" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><label>wære</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">sy</hi>. Ld. <hi rend="italic">sie</hi>. So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IIAs_10-1.attnote.fn.25" n="25" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">132</biblScope></bibl><label>noht</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">nawht</hi>. Ld. <hi rend="italic">nauht</hi>. Ot.</seg></note>
      </div>
